IEC60870.NETAsync — Changelog
=============================

Changes to version 6.0.2
------------------------
- fix(CS104): `ControlConfirmMatcher.ReadSelectBit` mis-read the Select bit for
  setpoint command confirmations. It always read the byte at `ASDU header + IOA`
  (correct only for C_SC/C_DC/C_RC, whose SCO/DCQ/RCO immediately follows the IOA).
  For C_SE_NA_1 / C_SE_NB_1 the 2-byte value precedes the QOS, and for C_SE_NC_1 a
  4-byte float precedes it — so the receive side read the low byte of the *value*
  instead of the QOS byte. When that byte's bit7 was set (e.g. normalized value
  0.5f -> 0xFF), the ACTIVATION_CON was keyed as select=true while the sender's key
  was select=false, the confirmation never matched, and the command timed out after
  `CommandConfirmationTimeout`. C_BO_TA_1 (no Select bit) was also mis-read.
  Fix: `SelectQualifierOffset(TypeID)` now returns the per-type qualifier offset
  (2 for C_SE_NA/NB, 4 for C_SE_NC, -1 = no Select bit) for the zero-alloc fast
  path, keeping it consistent with the typed `GetSelectBit(InformationObject)`.
  Added regression tests covering all 14 control types × select/execute plus value
  0.5f (they fail on the old behavior).
- perf(CS104): T1/T2/T3 定时从「每连接一个 `System.Threading.Timer`」改为进程级共享
  调度器 `SharedTimeoutScheduler`（单物理 Timer + 16 分片最小堆，按绝对到期时刻排序，
  惰性删除/代位校验，类比 Netty `HashedWheelTimer`）。各连接仍持有独立
  `APCIParameters`，由 `GetSuggestedDelayMs()` 给出各自的下一个检查时刻；`Iec104TimerScheduler`
  退化为注册句柄，对外语义不变（致命一次 onFatal、OCE/取消静默停止、瞬态异常继续）。
  10k 连接压测（16 核 Windows，cmd-interval 10ms 满载）：同 CPU 预算下吞吐 +12%
  （99.4k → 111.5k ASDU/s，复跑一致），每 ASDU CPU 成本 −12%（139.1µs → 122.0µs），
  命令 RTT p99 持平（23ms）；常规负载（cmd-interval 400ms）下 CPU −1.7%、p99 163→120ms、
  服务端处理异常 59→2。此前满载期 10k 连接的定时器自调度占整机 ~8.6% CPU（640k tick/s）。
  新增 10 个调度器功能测试（到期/重排/致命/取消/瞬态异常/200 连接异间隔/分片隔离等）。

Changes to version 6.0.1
------------------------
- TouchSocket dependency updated 4.3.6 -> 4.3.10 (CS101 and CS104; no API changes on our side).

Changes to version 6.0.0 (breaking)
-----------------------------------
- API renames for consistency between the zero-copy view and the heap model:
  `AsduView.CommonAddress` -> `AsduView.Ca` (matches `ASDU.Ca`),
  `AsduView.OriginatorAddress` -> `AsduView.Oa` (matches `ASDU.Oa`),
  `ApplicationLayerParameters.OA` -> `ApplicationLayerParameters.Oa`.
- New `ASDU(AsduView view)` constructor overload: materializes the zero-copy view
  into a heap ASDU (header fields assigned directly, information-object payload
  copied once) so it can outlive the receive buffer. Same validation as the
  byte[]-based constructor.
- TouchSocket dependency updated 4.3.2 -> 4.3.6.

Changes to version 4.0.9
------------------------
- Raw protocol frame events: unified `RawFrameReceived` / `RawFrameSent` on IEC 104 client/server and IEC 101 client/server. Complete single frame (APDU for 104 incl. 0x68 APCI header; FT1.2 frame for 101 incl. start/control/checksum), delivered as a freshly-copied byte[] that is safe to keep/queue/log. Fires only when a subscriber is attached (zero overhead otherwise). IEC 104 receive side upgraded from raw TCP chunks to reassembled complete APDUs (ApduReader.Frame + ApduFramer.FrameParsedHandler). IEC 101 LinkLayerEngine bridges its existing RawMessageHandler hooks into modern events.
- New example: examples/cs104-client-raw shows subscribing to raw frames on both IEC 104 (default) and IEC 101 (--101) clients.
- Aligned all three package versions to 4.0.9 (Core, CS101, CS104).

Changes to version 4.0.7
------------------------
- ASDU god class split: ASDU.cs is now a thin facade; encoding moved to AsduEncoder, decoding + TypeID registry to AsduDecoder (new AsduDecoding.cs)
- TypeID registry is now the single source of truth for payload sizes and decode dispatch; fixed 3 size/dedispatch drifts (M_BO_TB_1 10->12, C_CS_NA_1 5->7, M_PS_NA_1 wrong class)
- GetEncodedSize() is now derived from the TypeID registry (base class default) instead of ~60 per-class hardcoded overrides; only variable-size types (FileSegment) keep an override
- Encoding path 0GC: value objects (CP16/24/32/56Time2a, ScaledValue, BinaryCounterReading, StatusAndStatusChangeDetection) gained AsSpan(); all frame.AppendBytes(GetEncodedValue()) calls switched to span-based AppendBytes(AsSpan())
- LinkLayer class renamed to LinkLayerEngine (removes namespace/type name clash, drops the LinkLayerType alias hack)
- CS104/CS101 timer loops: silent exception swallowing replaced with diagnostic output
- Target net6.0; same public API surface as 4.0.6

